WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.339 --> 00:00:06.250
The military helicopter sailed through the
skies at a steady pace, its destination somewhere

00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:12.450
in Southwest Asia, along one of the many points
where the legendary Euphrates and Tigris rivers

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:13.450
meet.

00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:18.730
Depending on the outcome, this mission may
have changed the course of the SCP Foundation

00:00:18.730 --> 00:00:22.990
and its activities forever, or it might do
nothing at all.

00:00:22.990 --> 00:00:28.220
Such was often the way when it came to dealing
with the unpredictable and the anomalous.

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:34.050
Inside the helicopter, Dr. Anton Zharkov was
practically rattling with nervous excitement.

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:39.079
Ever since he’d been assigned to the 682
Termination Detail, after years of wasting

00:00:39.079 --> 00:00:45.020
away in an archival desk job, he’d seen
the kind of anomalies you wouldn’t believe.

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:49.719
173, that nightmarish statue that snaps the
necks of anyone who dared to look away from

00:00:49.719 --> 00:00:50.719
it.

00:00:50.719 --> 00:00:56.250
811, the strange and also strangely adorable
Swamp Woman, whose caustic mucus could reliably

00:00:56.250 --> 00:01:01.879
melt seemingly any organic matter - save,
of course, 682 itself.

00:01:01.879 --> 00:01:06.450
And Dr. Zharkov was particularly astonished
by the aftermath of the epic battle between

00:01:06.450 --> 00:01:13.359
096 and 682 , which left both of these “indestructible”
monsters horribly maimed.

00:01:13.359 --> 00:01:14.390
But all of that...

00:01:14.390 --> 00:01:18.069
It was nothing compared to what they were
going to witness today.

00:01:18.069 --> 00:01:21.929
Dr. Zharkov muttered a prayer to himself in
frightened reverence.

00:01:21.929 --> 00:01:26.299
Dr. Clef, who was sitting across from him
in the helicopter, wasn’t quite as wound

00:01:26.299 --> 00:01:27.299
up.

00:01:27.299 --> 00:01:31.859
Like some action movie cliche made manifest,
he sliced chunks from a plump, red apple with

00:01:31.859 --> 00:01:35.200
a Bowie knife and sucked the pieces off the
blade.

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:38.569
Clef found Zharkov’s nervousness little
more than amusing.

00:01:38.569 --> 00:01:40.759
“First time at Site 0, rookie?”

00:01:40.759 --> 00:01:42.549
Clef asked between apple slices.

00:01:42.549 --> 00:01:45.630
Dr. Zharkov nodded, forcing a meek smile.

00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:46.649
Clef just chuckled.

00:01:46.649 --> 00:01:50.770
“You’re wasting your time, you know,”
Clef said.

00:01:50.770 --> 00:01:52.459
“Everyone takes a shot at the reptile.

00:01:52.459 --> 00:01:57.249
I faced it down myself once, mano e mano,
and during that moment, I realized something.

00:01:57.249 --> 00:02:01.259
As much as it pains me to ever throw in the
towel, we’re not gonna kill this thing.

00:02:01.259 --> 00:02:03.159
It’s just a budget sink.”

00:02:03.159 --> 00:02:07.119
Of course, these kinds of doubts had crossed
Dr. Zharkov’s mind before.

00:02:07.119 --> 00:02:11.720
He’d watched countless termination attempts,
organized by far more senior researchers than

00:02:11.720 --> 00:02:15.080
himself, fail and fail embarrassingly.

00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:20.210
Something about signing your name up for 682
termination was like tying on a blindfold,

00:02:20.210 --> 00:02:25.560
grabbing a bat, and stepping up to a piñata,
except in this case, the piñata isn’t wearing

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:28.909
a blindfold, and somehow it can hit you back.

00:02:28.909 --> 00:02:34.170
It’s a one-way ticket to professional humiliation,
and if you’re unlucky enough to get too

00:02:34.170 --> 00:02:38.079
close when things go south, it can be so much
worse.

00:02:38.079 --> 00:02:43.900
But Dr. Zharkov well and truly believed that
he would be the exception to so much miserable

00:02:43.900 --> 00:02:44.900
failure.

00:02:44.900 --> 00:02:49.010
After all, this was an idea nobody had tried
before...

00:02:49.010 --> 00:02:53.190
An announcement over the intercom signaled
that they had now entered Site 0 airspace.

00:02:53.190 --> 00:02:55.140
They’d be landing shortly.

00:02:55.140 --> 00:03:00.530
And just like that, Dr. Zharkov was all raised
hairs and gooseflesh once again.

00:03:00.530 --> 00:03:05.000
It seemed like such a hazy, distant miracle
that his project proposal would even get majority

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:07.140
approval from the O5 Council.

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:10.900
And now, he was about to touch down and actually
see it.

00:03:10.900 --> 00:03:15.920
Naturally, Dr. Clef noticed Dr. Zharkov’s
emotional cues, and like so many playground

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:18.049
bullies, decided to seize on it.

00:03:18.049 --> 00:03:21.040
“Don’t buy into the hype,” Dr. Clef
said.

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:23.109
“It’s really not that special.”

00:03:23.109 --> 00:03:24.670
The helicopter touched down.

00:03:24.670 --> 00:03:29.959
Dr. Zharkov felt defensive, he was almost
tempted to use hard words, but he realized

00:03:29.959 --> 00:03:35.389
from Dr. Clef’s mischievous smile that perhaps
that was always the intention.

00:03:35.389 --> 00:03:37.870
He certainly had a...

00:03:37.870 --> 00:03:42.159
Reputation, if one were to put it in the most
neutral terms possible.

00:03:42.159 --> 00:03:46.629
“But this was your 001 proposal, Dr. Clef,”
Zharkov countered.

00:03:46.629 --> 00:03:49.930
“I would have thought you’d be more invested
in this.”

00:03:49.930 --> 00:03:54.329
Dr. Clef rose to his feet and sheathed his
Bowie knife as the helicopter’s side door

00:03:54.329 --> 00:03:55.329
opened.

00:03:55.329 --> 00:04:00.079
He gestured for Dr. Zharkov to get up and
follow him, before saying, “Believe me,

00:04:00.079 --> 00:04:05.079
even a giant flaming Demi-God loses its luster
when you need to write enough of those stupid

00:04:05.079 --> 00:04:06.400
reports on it.”

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:11.489
The two researchers disembarked from the helicopter
and walked into the legendary containment

00:04:11.489 --> 00:04:14.139
facility: Site 0.

00:04:14.139 --> 00:04:19.019
One of the most important and secretive containment
sites out there, even by the standards of

00:04:19.019 --> 00:04:22.130
the ever-clandestine SCP Foundation.

00:04:22.130 --> 00:04:26.139
If ever containment procedures failed here,
they’d be staring down the barrel of an

00:04:26.139 --> 00:04:32.410
unprecedented situation: A PATMOS XK-Class
End of the World Scenario.

00:04:32.410 --> 00:04:36.889
After all, they were dealing with one of the
most serious and powerful anomalies they’d

00:04:36.889 --> 00:04:38.330
ever contained here.

00:04:38.330 --> 00:04:42.770
Clef and Zharkov entered the control room,
filled with huge monitors displaying every

00:04:42.770 --> 00:04:47.590
kind of recordable metric, but the largest
screens were dominated by long-range drone

00:04:47.590 --> 00:04:54.240
footage of the iconic anomaly they were all
there to see: SCP-001, perhaps better known

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:56.560
as Uriel, The Gate Guardian.

00:04:56.560 --> 00:05:01.949
While Dr. Clef remained unfazed, Dr. Zharkov
felt a single tear crawling down his cheek.

00:05:01.949 --> 00:05:05.620
He had never seen an entity so utterly awe-inspiring.

00:05:05.620 --> 00:05:10.810
An impossibly tall, glowing humanoid entity
with eight great, fiery wings, and a glowing

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:15.521
blade made of pure heavenly fire, every bit
as hot as the sun.

00:05:15.521 --> 00:05:19.199
To think that such an incredible creature
existed on the same earth as him made him

00:05:19.199 --> 00:05:21.669
feel so incredibly small.

00:05:21.669 --> 00:05:26.610
The theories as to the creature’s true nature
were as myriad as they were unknowable.

00:05:26.610 --> 00:05:31.250
Some of the more devout among the Foundation’s
ranks even believe that he is a direct servant

00:05:31.250 --> 00:05:37.919
of the Abrahamic God, guarding the gate the
paradise, the Garden of Eden, Heaven itself.

00:05:37.919 --> 00:05:40.530
Dr. Clef just laughed.

00:05:40.530 --> 00:05:44.200
“Everything you hoped it’d be, Zharkov?”
he said.

00:05:44.200 --> 00:05:45.379
Dr. Zharkov nodded.

00:05:45.379 --> 00:05:47.699
“And more, Dr. Clef, and more.”

00:05:47.699 --> 00:05:53.169
Even from such a distance, the raw power of
the Gate Guardian is impossible to ignore.

00:05:53.169 --> 00:05:56.259
It radiates off of the being like an invisible
aura.

00:05:56.259 --> 00:06:00.940
Dr. Zharkov had read all the files, to get
within a kilometer of the mighty entity would

00:06:00.940 --> 00:06:02.909
be to court death.

00:06:02.909 --> 00:06:07.669
Anyone who approached it would taste the heat
of its sword, cleaving them apart at the atomic

00:06:07.669 --> 00:06:10.690
level and effectively erasing them from existence.

00:06:10.690 --> 00:06:17.380
It’s about as dead as anyone could possibly
be - Save for someone being thrown into SCP-3930

00:06:17.380 --> 00:06:20.520
and literally removed from the plane of existence.

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:24.460
SCP-3930 had failed to annihilate the Hard
to Destroy Reptile.

00:06:24.460 --> 00:06:29.639
But perhaps where that whole lot of nothing
had failed, the Gate Guardian would succeed.

00:06:29.639 --> 00:06:35.259
It remained floating, fixed on one place,
as though waiting for…

00:06:35.259 --> 00:06:36.449
Something.

00:06:36.449 --> 00:06:37.530
But what?

00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:42.870
Perhaps a fateful confrontation with a certain
reptilian nightmare, Dr. Zharkov hoped.

00:06:42.870 --> 00:06:48.030
Like many, he had heard the most famous story
involving SCP-001: The Gate Guardian, which

00:06:48.030 --> 00:06:51.970
took place before even the days of the SCP
Foundation.

00:06:51.970 --> 00:06:55.500
After all, every Foundation needs a Founder,
doesn’t it?

00:06:55.500 --> 00:06:57.229
And that’s how it began.

00:06:57.229 --> 00:07:00.919
The Founder was a mysterious figure, no matter
who you ask.

00:07:00.919 --> 00:07:05.470
Some say it was O5-1, others say it was the
legendary Administrator.

00:07:05.470 --> 00:07:11.340
Some even believe that it was someone else,
someone older, someone who predated even the

00:07:11.340 --> 00:07:14.449
current O5 Council and Administrator.

00:07:14.449 --> 00:07:19.710
A wise and learned figure, going on a pilgrimage
around the known world in hopes of expanding

00:07:19.710 --> 00:07:22.990
their perspective and seeking out the strange
and unusual.

00:07:22.990 --> 00:07:27.270
It was traveling down the River Tigris that
the Founder encountered the Gate Guardian

00:07:27.270 --> 00:07:30.300
- Of course, as always, from a mile away.

00:07:30.300 --> 00:07:34.930
The Founder saw the distant glowing point
shaped like a human being with wings.

00:07:34.930 --> 00:07:38.139
It was unlike anything they’d ever borne
witness to.

00:07:38.139 --> 00:07:42.780
That’s when the Founder felt a door open
in the back of their mind, and something sneak

00:07:42.780 --> 00:07:43.780
in.

00:07:43.780 --> 00:07:48.280
A single word, projecting somehow infinite
authority.

00:07:48.280 --> 00:07:50.160
“PREPARE.”

00:07:50.160 --> 00:07:53.689
The very presence of the word made the Founder’s
body rattle.

00:07:53.689 --> 00:07:58.150
Never had they heard such a voice, conveying
such certainty and power.

00:07:58.150 --> 00:08:02.530
It had to be the voice of the distant glowing
figure, it couldn’t be anything else, could

00:08:02.530 --> 00:08:03.530
it?

00:08:03.530 --> 00:08:08.310
Much like Dr. Zharkov would experience hundreds
of years later, the Founder, even as a person

00:08:08.310 --> 00:08:14.770
so powerful, knowledgeable, and influential,
suddenly felt so unimaginably small.

00:08:14.770 --> 00:08:20.409
The Founder became aware of not just the extent
of the world around them, or even the universe,

00:08:20.409 --> 00:08:23.650
but a terrifying multiverse of possibilities.

00:08:23.650 --> 00:08:27.350
There was light out there, of course, but
even more darkness.

00:08:27.350 --> 00:08:30.780
And terrifying things were hiding in the dark.

00:08:30.780 --> 00:08:32.090
Is that what “prepare” meant?

00:08:32.090 --> 00:08:36.590
Did it mean to be ready for all the terrible
things hiding in the dark, just waiting for

00:08:36.590 --> 00:08:38.640
the opportunity to strike?

00:08:38.640 --> 00:08:43.230
Just how great was the extent of the things
humanity didn’t understand out there?

00:08:43.230 --> 00:08:48.540
The Founder’s mind was flooded with so many
possibilities - If there was a tide of monsters

00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:53.560
in the blackness that needed to be fought
back, it was too much for any one person to

00:08:53.560 --> 00:08:54.790
ever handle.

00:08:54.790 --> 00:09:00.950
The Founder needed a group, all gathered around
the same mission: To contain the coming threat

00:09:00.950 --> 00:09:03.910
that the great glowing being had warned them
about.

00:09:03.910 --> 00:09:07.730
People of focus, commitment, and sheer willpower.

00:09:07.730 --> 00:09:11.880
People who would accept the knowledge of the
terrible things in the darkness and still

00:09:11.880 --> 00:09:15.640
not waver in the face of their great and noble
challenge.

00:09:15.640 --> 00:09:20.920
People who, if necessary, would be willing
to die in the dark so the rest of the human

00:09:20.920 --> 00:09:23.080
race would live in the light.

00:09:23.080 --> 00:09:30.080
They would be humanity’s greatest defenders,
even though they would defend in secret.

00:09:30.080 --> 00:09:32.680
This was how it had all begun, supposedly.

00:09:32.680 --> 00:09:37.510
Dr. Zharkov had heard the story whispered
many times while conducting his research into

00:09:37.510 --> 00:09:39.660
SCP-001.

00:09:39.660 --> 00:09:44.540
And now, here he stood, perhaps where the
Founder had been standing all those years

00:09:44.540 --> 00:09:45.540
ago.

00:09:45.540 --> 00:09:51.590
The SCP Foundation had faced down greater
threats than SCP-682 - The Hanged King, The

00:09:51.590 --> 00:09:56.290
Sealed King, The Scarlet King, hell, if they
wanted to, they could go toe to toe with the

00:09:56.290 --> 00:09:57.600
Burger King.

00:09:57.600 --> 00:10:02.010
And all of it had begun with a single word
from the mighty Gate Guardian.

00:10:02.010 --> 00:10:06.100
Surely an ornery, overgrown lizard wouldn’t
be too much for it to handle?

00:10:06.100 --> 00:10:10.420
But of course, they hadn’t just come here
to look at the Gate Guardian, that’d be

00:10:10.420 --> 00:10:13.360
an egregious waste of time and helicopter
fuel.

00:10:13.360 --> 00:10:20.160
They’d come here transporting precious cargo:
A chunk of SCP-682’s flesh, cut from the

00:10:20.160 --> 00:10:21.220
beast itself.

00:10:21.220 --> 00:10:25.920
Currently, it was attached to yet another
remote-controlled drone, set on a collision

00:10:25.920 --> 00:10:27.360
course for the Gate Guardian.

00:10:27.360 --> 00:10:32.980
Dr. Zharkov watched the video feeds with sweaty
palms as he saw the drone and its diabolical

00:10:32.980 --> 00:10:38.140
cargo enter the video’s view, getting closer
to the Gate Guardian by the moment.

00:10:38.140 --> 00:10:40.240
Closer, closer, closer.

00:10:40.240 --> 00:10:41.240
Until…

00:10:41.240 --> 00:10:44.160
The Gate Guardian struck out with its great
and terrible sword.

00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:49.030
For such an astronomically huge being to move
so incredibly fast was astounding in and of

00:10:49.030 --> 00:10:54.880
itself, but what Dr. Zharkov found even more
exciting was the result: In one quick slash

00:10:54.880 --> 00:11:01.970
of its solar blade, both the drone and the
SCP-682 tissue sample were utterly evaporated.

00:11:01.970 --> 00:11:05.760
Gone, reduced to less than even ash.

00:11:05.760 --> 00:11:08.990
Dr. Zharkov’s face split into a manic grin.

00:11:08.990 --> 00:11:14.980
If it could destroy the tissue sample, then
surely, it could destroy the monster itself,

00:11:14.980 --> 00:11:17.680
and what a glorious day that would be…

00:11:17.680 --> 00:11:24.020
Meanwhile, back at the cross-testing chambers
of Site-19, SCP-682 was having another miserable

00:11:24.020 --> 00:11:25.020
day.

00:11:25.020 --> 00:11:29.130
It was dragged, half-melted, out of its acid
tank at 3 AM in the morning and left slowly

00:11:29.130 --> 00:11:30.840
regenerating on the floor.

00:11:30.840 --> 00:11:37.290
A typical SCP Foundation wake-up call, it
thought to itself with a roll of its still-regenerating

00:11:37.290 --> 00:11:38.290
eyes.

00:11:38.290 --> 00:11:42.070
What form of horrible torment would be in
store for it this time?

00:11:42.070 --> 00:11:46.930
It began scrolling through its mental Rolodex
for the most recent failed-but-painful termination

00:11:46.930 --> 00:11:47.930
attempts.

00:11:47.930 --> 00:11:52.480
Oh, yes, of course, they’d tried suffocation
via vacuum!

00:11:52.480 --> 00:11:56.700
That definitely made SCP-682 feel a little
light-headed, at least.

00:11:56.700 --> 00:12:01.230
Until, of course, it adapted its body to begin
releasing a gas of similar composition to

00:12:01.230 --> 00:12:06.570
its native atmosphere, which had certainly
given those white-coat-wearing sadists a lot

00:12:06.570 --> 00:12:07.970
to take notes about.

00:12:07.970 --> 00:12:12.960
Then, how could it forget, they’d tried
roasting it to death with extremely high temperatures.

00:12:12.960 --> 00:12:17.790
Thankfully, as always, it’d had a trick
up its sleeve: Adapting a carapace made of

00:12:17.790 --> 00:12:22.800
solid helium to defend it from the fire, then
shattering it to shred a bunch of those buffoons

00:12:22.800 --> 00:12:24.130
in the orange jumpsuits.

00:12:24.130 --> 00:12:28.930
Then they’d cut off a sample of its flesh
shoved it into some absurd industrial blender

00:12:28.930 --> 00:12:31.550
before shoving what’s left into a centrifuge.

00:12:31.550 --> 00:12:37.241
What a divine pleasure it had been for 682
to hear the explosion down the hall, when

00:12:37.241 --> 00:12:41.570
the antimatter embedded in its jeans went
off and put a number of those idiotic Foundation

00:12:41.570 --> 00:12:43.950
drones in the hospital for months.

00:12:43.950 --> 00:12:47.941
Serves them right for continually meddling
in the matters of forces they couldn’t even

00:12:47.941 --> 00:12:49.810
hope to understand.

00:12:49.810 --> 00:12:51.060
And today…

00:12:51.060 --> 00:12:54.000
They were feeding it the carcass of a dead
cow.

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:55.940
SCP-682 sighed.

00:12:55.940 --> 00:13:00.690
It felt sometimes that the dolts testing it
had forgotten the note reading “Highly Intelligent”

00:13:00.690 --> 00:13:02.070
on its file.

00:13:02.070 --> 00:13:06.170
Being dragged into one of these ghastly chambers
and given some form of novel stimulus could

00:13:06.170 --> 00:13:11.860
only mean one thing: Something stupid and
painful was going to happen.

00:13:11.860 --> 00:13:16.190
Said stupid, painful thing, in this case,
was that the cow was spiked with an instance

00:13:16.190 --> 00:13:21.870
of SCP-3521 - also known as The Banana Pill,
by dado.

00:13:21.870 --> 00:13:28.600
What followed was a remarkably absurd instance,
even by SCP-682 cross-test standards, where

00:13:28.600 --> 00:13:32.910
a huge number of bananas spontaneously burst
out of 682’s body.

00:13:32.910 --> 00:13:37.740
Being a big fan of bananas, apparently, 682
was actually able to eat and metabolize the

00:13:37.740 --> 00:13:42.430
bananas faster than the anomalous Banana Pill
- by dado - could produce them.

00:13:42.430 --> 00:13:47.590
And because bananas are each, individually,
slightly radioactive, 682 was able to synthesize

00:13:47.590 --> 00:13:52.120
this collective radiation into a powerful
death ray that it used to cause a great deal

00:13:52.120 --> 00:13:54.050
of death and destruction.

00:13:54.050 --> 00:13:58.500
As far as Dr. Zharkov, and the rest of the
SCP Foundation, were concerned, this thing

00:13:58.500 --> 00:14:03.450
being cleaved apart on an atomic level by
the Gate Guardian couldn’t come soon enough.

00:14:03.450 --> 00:14:08.050
Sometimes, it took the ultimate knight to
slay the ultimate dragon.

00:14:08.050 --> 00:14:13.330
Not long after that, SCP-682 was dosed up
on enough sedatives to give New York City

00:14:13.330 --> 00:14:19.400
a week-long nap, and carted over to Site 0
on a heavily secured armored convoy.

00:14:19.400 --> 00:14:24.990
Taking SCP-682 this far between containment
sites was considered a matter of grave seriousness.

00:14:24.990 --> 00:14:29.810
In other words, the results of this little
experiment better have been good to justify

00:14:29.810 --> 00:14:34.630
the insane security risk it took to even get
the damn lizard out here.

00:14:34.630 --> 00:14:40.450
Dr. Zharkov and Dr. Clef decided to co-supervise
the cross test, from the safety of the Site

00:14:40.450 --> 00:14:41.860
0 observation deck.

00:14:41.860 --> 00:14:46.180
Either would have to be beyond foolish to
want to get any closer - Even Dr. Clef, while

00:14:46.180 --> 00:14:49.640
undeniably a loose cannon, didn’t have an
outright death wish.

00:14:49.640 --> 00:14:54.360
Unless, of course, wishing death on SCP-682
would count.

00:14:54.360 --> 00:14:59.710
682’s sedated body was strapped to a large,
unmanned vehicle - the kind they might use

00:14:59.710 --> 00:15:04.880
for an exploratory mission on another planet
- and sent in the direction of the Gate Guardian’s

00:15:04.880 --> 00:15:06.890
deadly proximal zone.

00:15:06.890 --> 00:15:11.640
A secondary camera drone was also sent in
to lag behind, correctly predicting that,

00:15:11.640 --> 00:15:16.920
when the Gate Guardian struck SCP-682, it
would obliterate the unmanned vehicle, too.

00:15:16.920 --> 00:15:21.090
And whatever happened out there, the Foundation
needed it on camera.

00:15:21.090 --> 00:15:26.420
Dr. Zharkov had sweaty palms and gritted teeth,
seeing the culmination of his professional

00:15:26.420 --> 00:15:28.330
career unfold in front of him.

00:15:28.330 --> 00:15:31.270
Dr. Clef was looking at a meme on his phone.

00:15:31.270 --> 00:15:37.000
As 682 got closer, it began hearing a booming
voice in its head, just like the Founder had

00:15:37.000 --> 00:15:38.710
so long ago.

00:15:38.710 --> 00:15:44.290
The voice simply said one word, over and over,
getting louder as the unmanned vehicle brought

00:15:44.290 --> 00:15:49.040
the two titans closer and closer and closer.

00:15:49.040 --> 00:15:50.720
“DIE.”

00:15:50.720 --> 00:15:57.310
682, still feeling groggy, thought, “Oh,
if it onlywere so simple…”

00:15:57.310 --> 00:16:02.680
And then it happened: SCP-682 entered the
dreaded one-kilometer range.

00:16:02.680 --> 00:16:07.220
The Guardian slashed down with its mighty
sword, creating a brilliant flash of light.

00:16:07.220 --> 00:16:12.280
In the aftermath, the unmanned vehicle was
obliterated, and 682 was left heavily injured

00:16:12.280 --> 00:16:15.850
on the ground, still trying to process what
had just happened.

00:16:15.850 --> 00:16:21.720
682 looked up, sobered by the pain, and saw
the being that had dealt this blow.

00:16:21.720 --> 00:16:23.660
682 began to sneer.

00:16:23.660 --> 00:16:26.400
“Is this meant to be the Garden?”

00:16:26.400 --> 00:16:30.130
it said, before breaking into a venomous laugh.

00:16:30.130 --> 00:16:34.550
“This is not the Garden.

00:16:34.550 --> 00:16:36.600
The Garden is far west of here.”

00:16:36.600 --> 00:16:42.060
The Gate Guardian struck again with its flaming
blade, once again projecting that single word,

00:16:42.060 --> 00:16:46.260
“DIE, DIE, DIE, DIE, DIE…”

00:16:46.260 --> 00:16:52.120
When the smoke cleared, 682 was even more
horrifically injured, with only one limb left,

00:16:52.120 --> 00:16:55.470
but still, against all odds, alive.

00:16:55.470 --> 00:17:00.770
It used the one limb to drag itself towards
the Gate Guardian, fueled by pure rage and

00:17:00.770 --> 00:17:01.770
spite.

00:17:01.770 --> 00:17:02.770
“Die?

00:17:02.770 --> 00:17:04.779
You command me to die?

00:17:04.779 --> 00:17:12.230
Oh, wouldn't we all like that, but this is
my curse for suggesting the fruit,” the

00:17:12.230 --> 00:17:13.640
reptile growled.

00:17:13.640 --> 00:17:16.659
Back at the base, Dr. Zharkov was mortified.

00:17:16.659 --> 00:17:18.970
How could it possibly be surviving all this?

00:17:18.970 --> 00:17:21.919
The sword was meant to cleave apart its victims
on an atomic level!

00:17:21.919 --> 00:17:22.919
Atomic!

00:17:22.919 --> 00:17:25.110
As in, freaking atoms, god damn it!

00:17:25.110 --> 00:17:28.069
Dr. Zharkov wished he had a paper bag to breathe
into.

00:17:28.069 --> 00:17:33.400
Dr. Clef, showing an uncharacteristic degree
of compassion, patted Zharkov on the back,

00:17:33.400 --> 00:17:37.470
saying, “It’s okay, buddy, we all remember
our first time.”

00:17:37.470 --> 00:17:42.000
Back at the center of the action, the Gate
Guardian blasted the 682 with its solar blade

00:17:42.000 --> 00:17:43.000
again.

00:17:43.000 --> 00:17:48.120
Somehow, despite the terrifying power wielded
by the Guardian, 682 continued to live.

00:17:48.120 --> 00:17:53.919
It was alive, barely, but after three strikes
from the sword, to be alive was whatever the

00:17:53.919 --> 00:17:57.019
evil version of a miracle would be.

00:17:57.019 --> 00:18:05.520
“This is not the Garden, and you are not
Uriel,” 682 roared, before spitting at the

00:18:05.520 --> 00:18:06.909
Gate Guardian.

00:18:06.909 --> 00:18:08.309
“Pretender.”

00:18:08.309 --> 00:18:13.850
One more violent strike from the Gate Guardian
and 682 finally collapsed, unconscious from

00:18:13.850 --> 00:18:16.750
the extent of its pain and its injuries.

00:18:16.750 --> 00:18:20.850
But despite all of Dr. Zharkov’s hopes,
the Gate Guardian did not strike a killing

00:18:20.850 --> 00:18:22.910
blow on the unconscious beast.

00:18:22.910 --> 00:18:30.629
Instead, it transmitted another word, another
order, impossible for any human being to ignore.

00:18:30.629 --> 00:18:32.250
“REMOVE.”

00:18:32.250 --> 00:18:38.309
As though in a trance, the workers of Site
0 - including Dr. Zharkov and Dr. Clef - entered

00:18:38.309 --> 00:18:41.580
the forbidden one-kilometer exclusion zone.

00:18:41.580 --> 00:18:46.019
The Gate Guardian allowed them safe passage,
as they used tools and vehicles to pick up

00:18:46.019 --> 00:18:51.920
the heavily injured SCP-682 and cart it away
from the Gate Guardian’s feet.

00:18:51.920 --> 00:18:56.660
After they all came back to their senses,
Dr. Zharkov simply said, “What just happened?”

00:18:56.660 --> 00:18:58.299
Dr. Clef just shrugged.

00:18:58.299 --> 00:19:00.429
“I’ve learned to stop questioning it.”

00:19:00.429 --> 00:19:06.879
Now go check out “SCP-001 - The Way The
World Ends - The Gate Opens” and “SCP-682

00:19:06.879 --> 00:19:11.590
- Ways SCP Foundation Tried to Kill Hard To
Destroy Reptile” for more madness from the

00:19:11.590 --> 00:19:14.799
two combatants featured in today’s epic
video!

